      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: record mobile KMP feasibility gates",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Android and Apple clients contain duplicated deterministic business rules, but the first KMP feasibility prototype showed that a local SwiftPM binary target backed by an untracked Gradle XCFramework breaks clean `OpenClawKit` package builds.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis plan now treats KMP/SKIE as an experiment pending Android and Apple owner sponsorship. It records the failed package-boundary model, requires a self-contained Apple package contract or an app-local boundary that leaves `OpenClawKit` independent, and requires a materially net-negative complete-domain extraction.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone. This is planning-only. Native UI ownership and current production behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- A clean worktree at the feasibility head failed `swift package build` for `apps/shared/OpenClawKit` because the local XCFramework artifact was absent.\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx`, `DOCS_I18N_GLOSSARY_BASE=upstream/main pnpm docs:check-i18n-glossary`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- The plan explicitly rejects a hidden Gradle pre-build as a SwiftPM package requirement and rejects a token `-4` production diff as a sufficient maintenance win.\n",
        "branch": "docs/mobile-kmp-native-ui-plan",
